# Computer-Assisted Instruction for Introductory Genetics.

**Authors:** Ferguson, N. H., Chapman, S. R.

## Abstract
Computer-assisted genetics instructor (CAGI) is a database program to help students and teachers identify conceptual weaknesses, provide interactive drill to master problem solving, and reduce teacher tutorial time. Results of a comparison of users and nonusers indicates that CAGI users averaged between 6 and 10 points higher on hour exams than nonusers. (MDH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ471493

